# OCEANBOUND — MAJOR WORLD, FLEET WARFARE, GHOST SHIPS, WEATHER AND GAMEPLAY UPDATE

Update the existing Oceanbound game with all the following changes.

**IMPORTANT: Preserve all existing gameplay and features unless specifically instructed to change or remove them.** Keep the existing ocean physics, shipwrecks, gold, trading, ship upgrades, pirate factions, Crown Fleet, sea monsters, crew management, fleet building, journal, music and simplified naval combat.

# 1. FIX AUTOMATIC CANNON FIRE

Fix the existing combat bug where cannons sometimes stop automatically firing when fighting anything other than pirate ships.

Automatic targeting and firing must work against EVERY hostile target, including:
- Pirate ships.
- Merchant and cargo ships that attack the player.
- The Crown Fleet when hostile.
- Sea monsters.
- Ghost Ships.
- Enemy fleets and flagships.
- Other hostile NPC vessels.

Cannons should automatically identify valid hostile targets, aim and fire when within range.

Make sure:
- Reload timers work correctly.
- Cannons retarget when enemies sink or escape.
- Different cannon types work correctly.
- Crew assignments affect reload speed.
- Enemy ships automatically fire at their targets.
- Cannonballs successfully hit sea monsters and Ghost Ships.

Combat must depend on whether something is hostile, not its ship category.

# 2. SIMPLIFY NAVAL COMBAT CONTROLS

Remove the bracing, defending and automatic escaping combat options.

The player should not need separate buttons to brace, defend or escape.

Keep naval combat simple:
- Cannons automatically aim and fire at hostile targets.
- The player manually steers using WASD.
- The player can manually attempt to escape by sailing away.
- Space gradually stops the ship.
- The only special combat option button should be SURRENDER.

### Manual escape

The player should simply turn their ship around and sail away using normal controls.

Do not display an escape button or automatically make the ship flee.

Enemies should pursue the player if appropriate. Escaping should depend on speed, steering, distance and enemy behaviour.

### Surrender button

Keep one clearly visible SURRENDER button during combat.

When pressed:
- Stop resisting.
- Allow the enemy to demand gold, resources or cargo.
- Deduct the agreed amount from the player's inventory.
- End the encounter if the enemy accepts.

Different enemies should make different surrender demands.

